Subject: [PATCH 44/44] docs: the Metal recipe serves with copy drafts and
 libtfgrammar

--no-drafts is no longer the only mode: copies are on by default and keep the
tokens of a --no-drafts run on the affine trees. The serve step builds
libtfgrammar from xgrammar v0.2.8, without which required and named tool calls
get HTTP 400, and says how --thinking-reserve keeps room for the answer when a
thinking budget would reach max_tokens.
---
 docs/recipes/sensenova-loop-9b-metal.md | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/recipes/sensenova-loop-9b-metal.md b/docs/recipes/sensenova-loop-9b-metal.md
index ad77016ad..2705c6507 100644
--- a/docs/recipes/sensenova-loop-9b-metal.md
+++ b/docs/recipes/sensenova-loop-9b-metal.md
@@ -45,16 +45,26 @@ Two mappings are not obvious and are the difference between working and garbage:
 
 ```bash
 zig build native -Dcpu=apple_m1
+git clone --branch v0.2.8 --recurse-submodules https://github.com/mlc-ai/xgrammar ../xgrammar
+zig build grammar -Dxgrammar=../xgrammar   # zig-out/native/lib/libtfgrammar.dylib
 zig-out/native/bin/tensorfold-native serve loop9b-mlx4 --name loop9b \
-  --context 2048 --prompt-cache-gib 0 --no-drafts
+  --context 33024 --parallel 4 --prompt-cache-gib 0
 ```
 
+`libtfgrammar.dylib` serves `tool_choice` required or named and `response_format`; without it those requests get
+HTTP 400. Check: a `tool_choice: "required"` request returns `finish_reason: tool_calls`, not 400.
+
 Load takes about 1.7 s for 4.72 GiB of weights. The model runs 56 decoder executions per token from 32 weight sets,
 so weights are read once and the graph walks the plan: `build: plan.linear 42 slots 8 cap 2048 steps 56 mhc true`.
 Each visit owns its KV and recurrent state, 14 attention and 42 linear slots.
 
-`--no-drafts` is the only supported mode: this checkpoint ships no drafter, and the loop's second visit is not a
-speculative path. Do not enable MTP or DFlash2 against it.
+Copy drafts are on by default: a stream drafts from its own context and the target verifies every draft, so on the
+affine q4 and q8 trees the tokens equal a `--no-drafts` run. `--no-drafts` turns them off. The checkpoint ships no MTP
+head; do not enable MTP against it.
+
+`--thinking-budget N` at or above a request's `max_tokens` never closes the thinking block before the reply runs out
+(`finish_reason: length`). Keep it under `max_tokens`, or add `--thinking-reserve N` to keep `max_tokens` for the
+answer.
 
